'''Shining Revelry''' (Japanese: '''シャイニングハイ''' ''Shining High'') is the third themed booster pack, and fifth expansion overall, in [[Pokémon Trading Card Game Pocket]].

== Information ==
'''Shining Revelry''' is the third themed booster pack released through [[Pokémon Trading Card Game Pocket]]. The expansion focuses on [[Shiny Pokémon]] and marks the first appearance of Pokémon and characters from [[Generation IX]] in the game.

Unlike previous Pokémon TCG Pocket booster packs, which each include five {{TCGP|Pokémon ex}} to collect, Shining Revelry includes nine instead (one of each type, excluding {{TCG|Dragon}}). This is due to the fact that, alongside the expansion, nine {{TCGP|ex Starter Decks}} were temporarily made available between March 28 and April 27, 2025, each relating to a different {{TCG|type}}, and each with a lead Pokémon ex. These are based on several real-world [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]] "Start Deck" products seen in Japan, such as the {{TCG|V Starter Decks}} and {{TCG|ex Start Decks}}. Players were able to redeem a Deck Ticket—of which only one was made available—for an ex Starter Deck, and would immediately receive all 20 cards in that deck as well as its theme deck list.

Several connected Pokémon within Shining Revelry featured artwork by the same artist. While this was more commonplace in expansions up to and including the EX Series, it has since been seen less often, primarily reserved for special expansions such as {{TCG|151}}. The following all feature artwork by the same artist and are all part of [[#Themed Collections|Themed Collections]]:

* {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Sprigatito|5}}, {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Floragato|6}}, and {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Meowscarada|7}} were all illustrated by [[mashu]] and are in the '''Sprigatito's Green Sprouting''' collection;
* {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Magmar|11}} and {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Magmortar|12}} were both illustrated by [[Miki Tanaka]] and are in the '''Magmar's Evolution''' collection;
* {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Dondozo|20}} and {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Tatsugiri|21}} form a combined illustration by [[Tomowaka]] and are in the '''Henchman and Boss?''' collection;
* {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Pawmi|26}}, {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Pawmo|27}}, and {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Pawmot|28}} were all illustrated by [[Saboteri]] and are in the '''Extra Electrifying''' collection;
* {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Abra|29}}, {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Kadabra|30}}, and {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Alakazam|31}} were all illustrated by [[Mousho]] and are in the '''Bewitching World''' collection;
* {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Gimmighoul|36}} and {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Gholdengo|57}} were both illustrated by [[HYOGONOSUKE]] and are in the '''Pile of Coins''' collection;
* {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Machoke|38}} and {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Machamp|39}} both feature previous artwork by [[Kouki Saitou]] and are in the '''1,000 Punches''' collection alongside {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Machop|37}};
* {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Hitmonlee|40}} and {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Hitmonchan|41}} both feature previous artwork by [[Tomokazu Komiya]] originating from the {{TCG|Team Up}} expansion and are in the '''Punching & Kicking''' collection;
* {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Ekans|45}} and {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Arbok|46}} both feature previous artwork by [[Midori Harada]] originating from the {{TCG|EX Sandstorm}} expansion and are in the '''Intimidating Patterns''' collection;
* {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Shroodle|50}} and {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Grafaiai|51}} were both illustrated by [[Krgc]] and are in the '''Deep Forest Poison Patterns''' collection;
* {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Tinkatink|52}} and {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Tinkatuff|53}} were both illustrated by [[miki kudo]] and are in the '''Huge Hammer''' collection alongside {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Tinkaton ex|54}};
* {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Varoom|55}} and {{TCG ID|Shining Revelry|Revavroom|56}} were both illustrated by [[Souichirou Gunjima]] and are in the '''Menacing Motor Noise''' collection.

